<title>GERMANY: GEHE -LLOYDS NON-CORE UNITS SOLD.</title>
<headline>GEHE -LLOYDS NON-CORE UNITS SOLD.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German pharmaceutical group Gehe AG made 230 million sterling by selling off non-core operations of its British unit Lloyds Chemists, Gehe said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The company said that through the sales, it had reduced its original purchase price of Lloyds of 685 million pounds by about a third and that it had fulfilled purchase conditions stipulated by British competition authorities.</p>
<p>Gehe also said it had decided on a new unified management structure for the British company.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
